My final recommendation
Start by implementing the registry, Docker adapter, and job/event model before building the polished UI. Once those contracts are stable, the React screens become relatively straightforward, and you can add pipeline visualization and debugging features without rewriting the lifecycle layer.
I would also keep the shared Kafka infrastructure under your existing Compose configuration and manage application services independently where possible. This allows you to rebuild S3 without accidentally recreating Kafka or disturbing every other running service.
